package dev.rotalex.lutter.codegen

/**
 * A Gradle plugin the generated project must apply, as opposed to a library it must depend on.
 *
 * The two are not interchangeable: a library is on the classpath because emitted source imports
 * something from it, and a plugin changes how the project *compiles* that source. A container whose
 * graph is generated by a compiler plugin is the second kind, and a project that depends on
 * `metro-runtime` without applying `dev.zacsweers.metro` builds into unresolved graph accessors.
 *
 * Kept apart from [GeneratedLibrary] rather than folded into it because the scaffold writes them
 * to different places — the `[libraries]`/dependencies tables against the `[plugins]` block and the
 * module's own `plugins {}` — and a single enum would force every consumer to remember which half
 * each entry belonged to.
 */
public enum class GeneratedPlugin {

    /**
     * `dev.zacsweers.metro`: the compiler plugin [Metro]'s graph is resolved by.
     *
     * `apply false` in the root build and applied in the shared module, the shape this scaffold
     * already uses for the Kotlin and Compose plugins: one classpath, one place a version lives.
     */
    Metro,
}
